Find $\cos C$ in the right triangle shown below.


[asy]
pair A,B,C;
A = (0,0);
B = (6,0);
C = (0,8);
draw(A--B--C--A);
draw(rightanglemark(B,A,C,10));
label("$A$",A,SW);
label("$B$",B,SE);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$10$",(B+C)/2,NE);
label("$6$",B/2,S);
[/asy]

Find the ordered pair $(x,y)$ if

\begin{align*}
x+y&=(5-x)+(5-y),\\
x-y&=(x-1)+(y-1).
\end{align*}

In rectangle $ABCD$, $AB = 6$ cm, $BC = 8$ cm, and $DE = DF$. The area of triangle $DEF$ is one-fourth the area of rectangle $ABCD$. What is the length in centimeters of segment $EF$? Express your answer in simplest radical form.

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(0,24)--(32,24)--(32,0)--cycle);
draw((13,24)--(32,5));
label("$A$",(0,24),W);
label("$B$",(0,0),W);
label("$C$",(32,0),E);
label("$D$",(32,24),E);
label("$E$",(13,24),N);
label("$F$",(32,5),E);
[/asy]

